  "Adherent Colonies on Blood Culture Bottle Glass": "Blood Culture (Slow Growth): Grow slowly in blood cultures (~5+ days) and characteristically form adherent colonies sticking to the glass surface of blood culture bottles and agar media. Identified via MALDI-TOF MS or biochemical panels.",
  "Aerotolerant Survival (Catalase + & Superoxide Dismutase +)": "Oxygen Tolerance & Short-Chain Fatty Acids: Produces catalase and superoxide dismutase to survive transient oxygen exposure during tissue invasion; succinic acid inhibits phagocytic killing.",
  "Afebrile with Clear Sensorium, Fixed Dilated Pupils, Dry Mouth & Respiratory Paralysis": "Foodborne Botulism (Preformed Toxin): 1–3 days post-ingestion; dizziness, blurred vision with fixed dilated pupils, dry mouth (anticholinergic signs), constipation, abdominal pain, no fever, clear sensorium , progressing to bilateral…",
  "Alginate Mucoid Capsule/Biofilm (Cystic Fibrosis Chronic Pneumonia)": "Adhesins & Alginate Capsule: Flagella, pili, LPS (endotoxin), and alginate (mucoid exopolysaccharide capsule/biofilm activated in CF lungs that blocks phagocytosis and antibiotics).",
  "Alkaline-Encrusted Cystitis & Struvite Stones": "Alkaline-Encrusted Cystitis: Chronic calcifying bladder inflammation caused by struvite deposition in persistently alkaline urine due to urease-producing C. urealyticum .",
  "Alpha Toxin (Phospholipase C / Lecithinase — Nagler Reaction +) → Gas Gangrene (Myonecrosis) & Massive Hemolysis": "Nagler Reaction: Detection of C. perfringens alpha-toxin (lecithinase) precipitation on egg yolk agar, inhibited by anti-alpha-toxin antibody.",
  "Alpha-Hemolytic (Green)": "Separating Viridans Strep from S. pneumoniae (Crucial Lab Step): Both form green alpha-hemolytic colonies on blood agar and are Catalase (-).",
