  "Burn Wounds, Hot-Tub Folliculitis, Swimmer's Ear / Malignant Otitis Externa (Diabetics)": "Ear & Eye Infections: External otitis ( \"swimmer's ear\" ), life-threatening invasive malignant external otitis in elderly/diabetic patients (cranial nerve/bone invasion), chronic otitis media, and sight-threatening corneal ulcers (contact lens trauma + contaminated water).",
  "Butterscotch / Caramel Odor": "Colony Size Differentiator on Blood Agar: S. anginosus Group (\"Small-Colony\" Species): Capnophilic (requires CO 2 and 48 hours of incubation), forming tiny pinpoint (<0.",
  "Butyrate Esterase (+) & Asaccharolytic (Does Not Ferment/Oxidize Sugars)": "Butyrate Esterase Test: Rapid enzymatic spot test differentiating M. catarrhalis (+) from morphologically identical Neisseria species (-).",
  "CAMP Test (+) (Arrowhead Hemolysis)": "Diffusible CAMP factor synergizes with S. aureus beta-lysin (sphingomyelinase C) on sheep blood agar to create an arrowhead-shaped zone of enhanced beta-hemolysis (classic for Group B Strep; also positive in Listeria).",
  "Carrión Disease (Biphasic: Acute Oroya Fever → Chronic Verruga Peruana)": "Oroya Fever & Verruga Peruana: The acute hemolytic bacteremic phase and chronic vascular skin-nodule phase of B. bacilliformis Carrión disease.",
  "Caseating Granulomas & Langhans Giant Cells": "Granuloma Formation & Latency: Infected macrophages secrete IL-12 and TNF-α , recruiting T cells and NK cells to differentiate into TH1 cells secreting IFN-γ (activating macrophage killing).",
  "Cat & Dog Bite Wounds (Rapid-Onset Cellulitis & Lymphadenitis <24–48 h)": "Animal Bite Wound Infection (Most Common): Rapidly developing localized cellulitis, pain, serous/purulent discharge, and regional lymphadenitis within 24–48 hours of a cat or dog bite/scratch (can progress to tenosynovitis, osteomyelitis, or necrotizing fasciitis).",
  "Cat-Scratch Disease (Benign Chronic Regional Lymphadenopathy in Children)": "Cat-Scratch Disease (Immunocompetent Children): Benign, usually self-limited chronic regional lymphadenopathy draining the scratch/bite site (rarely disseminates to liver, spleen, eye, or CNS).",
  "Catalase (-) Pleomorphic Gram-Positive Diphtheroid Rod": "Formerly classified as Corynebacterium haemolyticum , Arcanobacterium haemolyticum is a facultatively anaerobic, catalase-negative, beta-hemolytic pleomorphic Gram-positive rod (diphtheroid) highlighted in Murray Chapter 79 as an important…",
