  "Cavitary Pneumonia + Brain Abscess Dissemination in Immunocompromised Hosts": "CNS Dissemination (Up to 1/3 of Patients!): Hematogenous spread from the lungs produces single or multiple brain abscesses (fever, headache, focal neurologic deficits, seizures) or chronic meningitis.",
  "Cellulitis, Soft-Tissue Infections & Osteomyelitis": "Site-Specific Endogenous Infections: Upper airway/oral → sinusitis, brain abscess, pleuropulmonary abscess ; GI → intraabdominal abscess ; GU → endometritis, salpingitis, pelvic/tubo-ovarian abscess ; Skin → cellulitis, soft-tissue…",
