  "Cervicofacial (Most Common — Jaw/Neck After Dental Procedure), Thoracic, Abdominal, Pelvic (IUD!) & Solitary Brain Abscess": "Cervicofacial Actinomycosis (Most Common): Follows poor oral hygiene, dental extraction, or oral trauma; painless or pyogenic woody jaw/neck swelling with draining sinus tracts along the jaw angle discharging yellow sulfur granules.",
  "Chancroid (Soft Chancre — Painful Genital Ulcer + Inguinal Lymphadenopathy)": "Soft Chancre (Chancroid): Painful, non-indurated genital ulcer with inguinal lymphadenopathy caused by H. ducreyi (\"you cry with ducreyi\").",
  "Chest X-Ray Patchy Infiltrates Worse Than Physical Exam": "Primary Atypical (\"Walking\") Pneumonia: Patchy bronchopneumonia on chest radiograph that looks markedly worse than clinical auscultation findings (GI symptoms/myalgias uncommon).",
  "Chocolate Agar & Modified Thayer-Martin Media (5% CO2)": "Modified Thayer-Martin Agar: Selective chocolate agar containing antibiotics (vancomycin, colistin, nystatin, trimethoprim) to isolate pathogenic Neisseria from mucosal sites.",
  "Chocolate Agar & Satellite Phenomenon Around S. aureus": "Culture (Chocolate Agar & Satellite Phenomenon): Sheep blood agar contains inhibitors of V factor; heating destroys these inhibitors, making chocolate agar required (overheating destroys V factor!",
  "Cholera Toxin (CTXΦ Phage — AB5 Toxin Binding GM1 → ↑cAMP)": "Cholera Toxin ( ctxA/ctxB on Phage CTX&Phi;): Classic AB 5 exotoxin homologous to ETEC LT-I.",
