  "Chronic Indolent Foreign-Body / VP Shunt / Prosthetic Joint & Valve Infections": "Opportunistic Foreign-Body Infections: Chronic, often afebrile CSF (VP) shunt meningitis , prosthetic joint/valve infections, intravascular catheter sepsis, and lacrimal canaliculitis.",
  "Chronic Q Fever (>6 Months): Blood-Culture-Negative Subacute Endocarditis (Phase I Antibodies Predominate — High Risk on Damaged Valves)": "Chronic Q Fever (>6 Months): Strikes patients with valvular heart disease or immunosuppression—classically presenting as serious blood-culture-negative subacute endocarditis .",
  "Citrobacter koseri: Strong Predilection for Neonatal Meningitis & Brain Abscesses": "Citrobacter koseri Neonatal CNS Disease: Distinct predilection for neonatal meningitis complicated by necrotic brain abscesses .",
