  "Classic Triad: Afebrile Presentation + Marked Hemoconcentration + Leukemoid Reaction": "Leukemoid Reaction: Extreme reactive elevation in peripheral white blood cell count (>50,000/μL) typical of C. sordellii toxic shock syndrome.",
  "Clinical Diagnosis; Treat Immediately with Debridement + Metronidazole + Human Tetanus IG + Toxoid Vaccine": "Four-Pillar Immediate Management: (1) Wound debridement , (2) Metronidazole (preferred over penicillin because penicillin antagonizes GABA and can worsen CNS excitability), (3) Human Tetanus Immunoglobulin (HTIG) to neutralize unbound…",
  "Club-Shaped / Chinese-Letter Pleomorphic Rods": "Corynebacterium diphtheriae is an irregularly staining, pleomorphic, club-shaped Gram-positive rod (arranged in palisades or \"Chinese-letter\" V/L formations).",
