  "Coagulase (-)": "Lacks free extracellular coagulase (negative tube coagulase test), distinguishing coagulase-negative staphylococci (e.g., S. epidermidis, S. saprophyticus, S. lugdunensis) from S. aureus.",
  "Coagulase (+)": "Produces bound clumping factor and free coagulase, converting plasma fibrinogen into an insoluble fibrin clot—the key lab test separating S. aureus (+) from all coagulase-negative staphylococci (-).",
  "Cold Enrichment (Grows at 4°C — Refrigerated Blood Transfusion Bacteremia/Shock)": "Cold Enrichment (4°C): Because Y. enterocolitica grows slowly at 37°C, mixing stool in saline at 4°C for ≥2 weeks selectively enriches it while killing competing flora.",
  "Cold Enrichment (Grows at 4°C)": "Cold Enrichment: Refrigerating specimens (4°C) to allow psychrotrophic Listeria to multiply while suppressing competing flora.",
  "Common Blood Culture Skin Contaminant (Evaluate Clinical Context Carefully!)": "Anaerobic Culture (Slow Growth): Requires 2–5+ days on anaerobic media; pleomorphic Gram-positive rods in clumps/short chains. Always interpret blood isolates alongside clinical context (foreign body vs. skin contaminant).",
  "Congenital Syphilis (Rhinitis, Desquamating Rash, Teeth/Bone Malformations, Blindness, Deafness)": "Congenital Syphilis: Fetal death or rhinitis, desquamating rash, teeth/bone malformations, blindness, deafness, and cardiovascular disease.",
  "Conjugate Vaccine (A, C, Y, W135) & Protein-Based Serogroup B Vaccine": "Vaccines: Quadrivalent conjugate vaccines cover serogroups A, C, Y, and W135 . Because serogroup B polysaccharide is weakly immunogenic and cross-reacts with human neural tissue, two separate protein-based serogroup B vaccines are approved.",
  "Contact Lens Corneal Ulcers & Nail-Puncture Foot Osteochondritis": "Ear & Eye Infections: External otitis ( \"swimmer's ear\" ), life-threatening invasive malignant external otitis in elderly/diabetic patients (cranial nerve/bone invasion), chronic otitis media, and sight-threatening corneal ulcers (contact lens trauma + contaminated water).",
  "Contaminated Poultry (>50% of Cases) & Unpasteurized Milk": "Epidemiology: Zoonotic and the most common cause of bacterial gastroenteritis in developed and developing countries (~1.",
  "Cornerstone: Prompt Fluid & Electrolyte Replacement + Single-Dose Azithromycin": "Fluid & Electrolyte Replacement (Life-Saving Cornerstone): Immediate aggressive oral or IV rehydration prevents shock and reduces mortality to <1%.",
  "Culture Blood/CSF in First 10 Days; Urine After Week 1 (Up to 3 Months) on Fletcher/EMJH Media at 28–30°C": "Specialized Culture Timing: Slow-growing (2 weeks to 4 months on Fletcher/EMJH media at 28–30°C). Collect blood or CSF during the first 10 days , and neutralized/centrifuged urine after week 1 (up to 3 months) .",
